  "solution": {
    "text": "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & \\sin \\theta & 1 \\\\ -\\sin \\theta & 1 & \\sin \\theta \\\\ -1 & -\\sin \\theta & 1\\end{array}\\right]$<br>$\\Rightarrow \\operatorname{det}(A)=\\left(11+\\sin ^2 \\theta\\right)-\\sin \\theta(-\\sin \\theta+\\sin \\theta)+1\\left(\\sin ^2 \\theta+1\\right)$<br>$=2+2 \\sin ^2 \\theta$<br>$\\because \\theta \\in\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}, \\frac{5 \\pi}{4}\\right)$<br>$\\therefore \\sin 2 \\theta \\in\\left[0, \\frac{1}{2}\\right]$<br>$\\therefore \\operatorname{det}(A) \\in[2,3]$ which is a subset of $\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, 3\\right]$"
